WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.670
The book of Exodus says the
sea went back all night,

2
00:00:03.720 --> 00:00:06.360
driven by a strong east wind.

3
00:00:06.410 --> 00:00:08.180
Wind is weather.

4
00:00:08.230 --> 00:00:11.190
So where, exactly, is the miracle?

5
00:00:11.240 --> 00:00:16.990
In 1748, the philosopher David Hume set
a very high bar for believing any miracle

6
00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:18.110
report.

7
00:00:18.160 --> 00:00:21.610
So if the sea parted
by a strong east wind,

8
00:00:21.660 --> 00:00:24.470
was it a miracle, or just weather?

9
00:00:24.520 --> 00:00:29.210
In this mission, you'll compare three
Jewish accounts of what a miracle is.

10
00:00:29.260 --> 00:00:32.320
Then you'll put Jewish
thinkers in dialogue with Hume,

11
00:00:32.370 --> 00:00:34.900
and with the theologian Maurice Wiles.

12
00:00:34.950 --> 00:00:40.050
Your mission: find out how Jewish
thinkers decide what counts as a miracle.
